Phonons via DFPT (answers reviewer R7: "no phonon calculations provided")
&inputph
  prefix   = '<<PREFIX>>'
  outdir   = './out'
  fildyn   = '<<PREFIX>>.dyn'
  tr2_ph   = 1.0d-14        ! phonon self-consistency threshold
  ldisp    = .true.         ! phonons on a q-grid (for full dispersion + DOS)
  nq1 = 2, nq2 = 2, nq3 = 2 ! q-mesh; use 1 1 1 for Gamma-only molecular crystal
  epsil    = .true.         ! dielectric + Born charges (IR, LO-TO splitting)
/
! After ph.x:
!   q2r.x   -> real-space force constants (<<PREFIX>>.fc)
!   matdyn.x -> phonon dispersion along a path + phonon DOS
!
! Electron-phonon coupling (reviewer R3, "strong e-ph coupling unsupported"):
!   for metals/semiconductors use the EPW code (Wannier interpolation) on top of
!   this DFPT run; for localised-state / molecular scintillators the relevant
!   quantity is the Huang-Rhys factor -> see huang_rhys.md.
